# round 98 (w116): the solver-free recipe with TWO media instead of one or four. Round 95 measured one medium with the counts and no solve at 0.888, against 0.902 for the same counts on four media and 0.916 for one medium with the solve. So once the solve is gone the extra media carry something; this asks how much of it the FIRST extra medium carries, which is the cheapest way to buy it back while keeping the record small. YPD is the medium the labels come from; SC is the one the alternative store was built on. Six seeds on the released split and the five folds, against 0.888 (one medium) and 0.902 (four).
ESS_SOLVE_TABLE=/scratch/projects/torchcell-scratch/data/torchcell/reference_flux/ess_solve_encodings_YPD_gpronly.npz ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_fold3of5_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2700 ESS_TAG=_w116twomedcv3 ESS_OUT=w116_twomedcv3_h12l1p1_e200_s2700 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --ess-readout fba --ess-fba-media YPD SC --ess-solve-features pfba --ess-solve-encoding log1p'
